# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY config/ ./config/`, which without this file would
# bake `config/secret_salt` into the image. The image is built on a connected
# machine and shipped to the air-gapped host as a `docker save` tarball, so the
# salt would travel with it — and leaking the salt makes every hashed
# identifier reversible by anyone who knows the organisation's email
# convention. Both README.md and comms_dashboard/config.py state that the salt
# is held outside the image; this is what makes that true.
#
# The salt is generated on first run inside the container, into the bind-mounted
# config/ directory, so excluding it here costs nothing operationally.
config/secret_salt

# Company data. data/samples/ is deliberately not excluded — the Dockerfile
# copies it so a fresh install has something to demonstrate with — but every
# directory that holds real exports is.
data/inbox/
data/archive/
data/rejected/
data/warehouse/
data/exports/

# Not needed in the image, and large.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tests/
docs/
profiles/
.DS_Store
